# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Bouncing Forward — environment variables
# Copy this file to `.env.local` (never commit .env.local) and
# fill in the values. On Vercel, add the same variables under
# Project → Settings → Environment Variables, then redeploy.
# Optional lines ship commented out (#) — uncomment only when
# you give them a value; never leave a variable as `NAME=`.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Mailchimp (newsletter + assessment sign-ups + buyers) ────

# API key — Mailchimp: profile icon → Account & billing →
# Extras → API keys → Create A Key.
MAILCHIMP_API_KEY=

# Audience ID — Audience → All contacts → Settings →
# Audience name and defaults → "Audience ID".
MAILCHIMP_AUDIENCE_ID=

# Server prefix — the part AFTER the dash in your API key
# (e.g. "us21"). Optional: derived from the key if omitted.
# MAILCHIMP_SERVER_PREFIX=

# ── Premium (the $9.99 Book Package) ─────────────────────────

# Access codes — comma-separated, case-insensitive. The first
# one is the canonical code handed to buyers right after
# payment; the same code goes into the confirmation email where
# it says [ACCESS CODE].  Example: BF-FORWARD-2026
PREMIUM_ACCESS_CODES=

# ── Supabase accounts (see docs/accounts-setup.md) ───────────

# Project URL + publishable key — Supabase → Project Settings →
# API. Safe for the browser; all reads run under Row Level
# Security.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# Secret key — same page. SERVER ONLY: used solely by the Stripe
# webhook to write entitlements. Never expose it to the browser.
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=

# ── Stripe (see docs/stripe-setup.md for the walkthrough) ────

# Price ID of the $9.99 product — Stripe → Product catalogue →
# the Book Package → its price → "API ID" (starts price_…).
# Checkout is created per-buyer by the site, tied to their
# account; test → live is just swapping this + the secret key.
STRIPE_PRICE_PREMIUM=

# Legacy Payment Link — no longer used by the buy buttons (the
# account flow replaced it); keep only if you still share the
# raw link anywhere.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PAYMENT_LINK=

# Secret key — Stripe → Developers → API keys ("sk_live_…",
# or "sk_test_…" while testing). Lets the site confirm a
# payment and open everything immediately after checkout.
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=

# Webhook signing secret — created with the webhook endpoint
# (Developers → Webhooks → your endpoint → "Signing secret",
# "whsec_…"). Lets Stripe tell the site about each sale so the
# buyer is tagged "premium" in Mailchimp (access-code email).
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# ── Formspree (contact form delivery) ────────────────────────

# The form's endpoint URL from formspree.io, e.g.
# https://formspree.io/f/abcdwxyz — with it set, the contact
# form sends for real; without it, Send opens the visitor's
# own mail app instead (the current behaviour).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FORMSPREE_ENDPOINT=

# ── Site URL ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Optional override for share images/links. Defaults to
# https://bouncing-forward.vercel.app; set when the real
# domain goes live.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=
